# Accessibility (WCAG 2.1 AA)

## Semantic HTML

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD — semantic elements
<nav aria-label="Main navigation">
<main>
<section aria-labelledby="trending-heading">
<h2 id="trending-heading">Trending Beats</h2>

// ❌ BAD — div soup
<div className="nav">
<div className="main">
<div className="section">
```

## ARIA labels

- Every interactive element without visible text needs `aria-label`.
- Icon-only buttons: `<Button aria-label="Play beat">`.
- Form inputs: pair with `<label>` or `aria-label`.
- Dynamic content: use `aria-live` for toast/status updates.

## Keyboard support

- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible.
- Visible focus indicators on every focusable element (`focus-ring` utility).
- Modal dialogs trap focus and close on `Escape`.
- Custom components: proper `role`, `tabIndex`, arrow key navigation.

## Screen readers

- Images: descriptive `alt` text (not "image", not empty unless decorative).
- Decorative images: `alt=""` and `aria-hidden="true"`.
- Links: descriptive text (not "click here").
- Status messages: `role="status"` or `aria-live="polite"`.

## Color and contrast

- Minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text.
- Minimum 3:1 for large text and UI components.
- Never convey information with color alone — use icons/text too.

## Reduced motion

```typescript
// ✅ Respect user preferences
className="motion-safe:transition-transform motion-reduce:transition-none"
```
